IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcimr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- Part 2, injury from employment: the prescribed
-- diseases and prescribed employment of Schedule 1 (reg 5), their qualifying periods (reg 6), the day the injury is taken
-- to be suffered (reg 7), the 1 July 2024 start (reg 8), COVID-19 (reg 9), post-traumatic stress disorder (reg 10), and the
-- cancers the regulations add to the firefighter diseases of s 11 of the Act (reg 11).
--
-- SEAT: the worker with the disease (or, where the worker has died of it, the worker's dependants). Every question is one
-- that person asks: "Is my disease taken to be from my work?", "On what day am I taken to have suffered it?".
--
-- What the presumption is (Act s 10(2)): "If a worker suffers an injury by a prescribed disease and the employment in which
-- the worker works at the time of suffering the injury, or in which the worker worked at any time before suffering the
-- injury, is prescribed employment for the disease, the injury is taken to be injury from that employment unless the
-- employer proves that the injury was not from that employment." Whether my work is of the kind column 2 describes is a
-- fact the person states; whether the employer proves otherwise is a judgment for the arbitrator, asked as a fact. Without
-- the presumption the injury can still be shown to be from employment (s 10(5)); these questions answer only for s 10.
--
-- Edition: compilation version 00-c0-00, current from 30 June 2026 (mrdoc 49606), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49606.txt. Schedule 1 as amended by SL 2024/89.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 19 October 2026, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- Part 2, diseases taken to be from employment`

§§ `reg 7 -- the day the injury is taken to be suffered`

-- Reg 7: "A worker who suffers an injury by a prescribed disease is taken to have suffered the injury -- (a) on the day on
-- which the worker is first diagnosed with the prescribed disease by a medical practitioner; or (b) if the worker dies as a
-- result of the prescribed disease before they are diagnosed as described in paragraph (a) -- on the day on which the
-- worker dies."
GIVEN `the day of first diagnosis` IS A DATE
      `the worker died of it before diagnosis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the injury day under reg 7` MEANS
    IF `the worker died of it before diagnosis`
    THEN `the day of death`
    ELSE `the day of first diagnosis`

@export On what day am I taken to have suffered my injury by a prescribed disease (reg 7)?
GIVEN `the day I was first diagnosed` IS A DATE @desc The day a medical practitioner first diagnosed you with the disease (any day if you were never diagnosed)
      `the worker died of the disease before diagnosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died of the disease before any diagnosis (asked by the worker's dependants)
      `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of death (any day if the worker has not died)
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day am I taken to have suffered my disease` MEANS
    `the injury day under reg 7` `the day I was first diagnosed` `the worker died of the disease before diagnosis` `the day the worker died`

§§ `regs 5, 6, 8 and Schedule 1 -- prescribed diseases`

-- Schedule 1, column 1, in the Table's order. Item 4 (COVID-19) and item 37 (post-traumatic stress disorder) have their own
-- conditions (regs 9 and 10) and their own questions below. Item 25 (liver) has two kinds of prescribed employment, (a) and
-- (b), with different periods, so it is two choices here.
DECLARE `Prescribed disease` IS ONE OF
    `Anthrax`
    `Avian Influenza`
    `Brucellosis`
    `Hepatitis A`
    `Hepatitis B or C`
    `HIV/AIDS`
    `Influenza A (H1N1)`
    `Leptospirosis`
    `Middle East Respiratory Syndrome`
    `Orf`
    `Psittacosis`
    `Q-fever`
    `Tuberculosis`
    `Primary leukaemia`
    `Primary malignant disease of the bile duct`
    `Primary malignant disease of the bladder`
    `Primary malignant disease of the bone`
    `Primary malignant disease of the brain`
    `Primary malignant disease of the breast (female)`
    `Primary malignant disease of the colon or rectum`
    `Primary malignant disease of the eye (melanoma)`
    `Primary malignant disease of the kidney`
    `Primary malignant disease of the larynx`
    `Primary malignant disease of the liver, from bodily secretions and hepatitis B or C exposure`
    `Primary malignant disease of the liver, from vinyl chloride monomer exposure`
    `Primary malignant disease of the lung`
    `Primary malignant disease of the nasal cavity or paranasal sinuses`
    `Primary malignant disease of the nasopharynx`
    `Primary malignant disease of the oesophagus`
    `Primary malignant disease of the ovary`
    `Primary malignant disease of the salivary gland`
    `Primary malignant disease of the skin (melanoma)`
    `Primary malignant disease of the skin (non-melanoma)`
    `Primary malignant disease of the stomach`
    `Primary malignant disease of the thyroid`
    `Primary non-Hodgkin lymphoma`
    `Peripheral neuropathy`
    `Byssinosis`
    `Extrinsic allergic alveolitis`
    `Obliterative bronchiolitis`
    `Occupational asthma`
    `Chronic active hepatitis`
    `Hepatic cirrhosis`
    `Non-infectious hepatitis`
    `Contact dermatitis (irritant and allergic)`
    `Occupational vitiligo`
    `Bursitis (at the elbow or knee)`
    `Osteonecrosis`
    `Raynaud's disease`
    `Poisoning or toxicity causing acute damage to the heart, lungs, liver, kidney, nervous system or blood`
    `A disease not listed in Schedule 1`

-- Reg 6(1): "Employment for a period (a qualifying period) specified in column 2 of the Table in Schedule 1 is a condition
-- on the operation of section 10 of the Act." The periods column 2 states: "for at least 2 years" (items 15, 36), "for
-- at least 5 years" (items 16-24, 25(b), 26-35), "for at least 1 year" (items 38, 45), "for at least 4 weeks" (items
-- 39-42, 46, 47), "for at least 6 months" (items 43, 48), "for at least 12 weeks" (item 50); the other items state none.
DECLARE `Qualifying period` IS ONE OF
    `no qualifying period`
    `at least this many weeks` HAS `the weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `at least this many months` HAS `the months` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Prescribed disease`
GIVETH A `Qualifying period`
`the qualifying period for` `the disease` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the disease`
    WHEN `Primary leukaemia` THEN `at least this many months` 24
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the bile duct` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the bladder` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the bone` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the brain` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the breast (female)` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the colon or rectum` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the eye (melanoma)` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the kidney` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the larynx` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the liver, from vinyl chloride monomer exposure` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the lung` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the nasal cavity or paranasal sinuses` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the nasopharynx` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the oesophagus` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the ovary` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the salivary gland` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the skin (melanoma)` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the skin (non-melanoma)` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the stomach` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary malignant disease of the thyroid` THEN `at least this many months` 60
    WHEN `Primary non-Hodgkin lymphoma` THEN `at least this many months` 24
    WHEN `Peripheral neuropathy` THEN `at least this many months` 12
    WHEN `Byssinosis` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Extrinsic allergic alveolitis` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Obliterative bronchiolitis` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Occupational asthma` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Chronic active hepatitis` THEN `at least this many months` 6
    WHEN `Non-infectious hepatitis` THEN `at least this many months` 12
    WHEN `Contact dermatitis (irritant and allergic)` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Occupational vitiligo` THEN `at least this many weeks` 4
    WHEN `Bursitis (at the elbow or knee)` THEN `at least this many months` 6
    WHEN `Raynaud's disease` THEN `at least this many weeks` 12
    OTHERWISE `no qualifying period`

-- Reg 6(3): "A qualifying period is satisfied if, on the day on which the injury is taken, under regulation 7, to have been
-- suffered, the worker (whether or not still in the prescribed employment) has completed a period of the prescribed
-- employment of, or 2 or more periods of prescribed employment in aggregate amounting to, the qualifying period".
GIVEN `the period` IS A `Qualifying period`
      `complete months` IS A NUMBER
      `complete weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualifying period` `the period` `is met by` `complete months` `months or` `complete weeks` `weeks` IF
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `no qualifying period` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `at least this many weeks` n THEN `complete weeks` AT LEAST n
    WHEN `at least this many months` n THEN `complete months` AT LEAST n

-- Reg 5: a disease in column 1 "is a prescribed disease" and the employment in column 2 "is prescribed employment for that
-- disease". Reg 6(2): "Section 10 of the Act does not apply to an injury by a prescribed disease unless any qualifying
-- period ... is satisfied." Reg 8: "section 10 of the Act does not apply to an injury by a prescribed disease suffered by a
-- worker unless the day on which the injury is taken, under regulation 7, to have been suffered is on or after 1 July
-- 2024." Act s 10(2): "... unless the employer proves that the injury was not from that employment."
-- A disease not in Schedule 1 is not a prescribed disease, so s 10 gives no presumption for it (fork F4: the other reading
-- is NOTHING, the list not being closed with "only").
@export Is my disease taken to be from my employment under s 10 of the Act, as a prescribed disease in Schedule 1 (regs 5-8)?
GIVEN `my disease` IS A `Prescribed disease` @desc Your disease, as Schedule 1 names it (COVID-19 and post-traumatic stress disorder have questions of their own; choose "A disease not listed in Schedule 1" if it is not there)
      `my work is or was of the kind Schedule 1 lists for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work you do, or did at any time before the injury, is of the kind of employment column 2 of Schedule 1 describes for your disease (for example work with animals or animal carcasses, or exposure to the substance named)
      `complete months in that kind of work` IS A NUMBER @desc The complete months you had worked in that kind of employment, in total over all periods, by the day you are taken to have suffered the injury
      `complete weeks in that kind of work` IS A NUMBER @desc The same total in complete weeks
      `the day I was first diagnosed` IS A DATE @desc The day a medical practitioner first diagnosed you with the disease (any day if never diagnosed)
      `the worker died of the disease before diagnosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died of the disease before any diagnosis
      `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of death (any day if the worker has not died)
      `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has proved to an arbitrator that the injury was not from that employment (for example that the employment did not contribute to a significant degree)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disease taken to be from my employment` IF
        `my disease is prescribed`
    AND `my work is or was of the kind Schedule 1 lists for it`
    AND `the qualifying period` (`the qualifying period for` `my disease`) `is met by` `complete months in that kind of work` `months or` `complete weeks in that kind of work` `weeks`
    AND `the injury day` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2024)
    AND (NOT `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment`)
    WHERE
        `my disease is prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my disease`
            WHEN `A disease not listed in Schedule 1` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the injury day` MEANS `the injury day under reg 7` `the day I was first diagnosed` `the worker died of the disease before diagnosis` `the day the worker died`

§§ `reg 9 -- COVID-19`

DECLARE `COVID-19 employment` IS ONE OF
    `a health professional`
    `any work in a hospital, medical practice, clinic or facility for health screening, testing or treatment`
    `an ambulance officer`
    `other work`

-- Reg 9(2): the prescribed employment for COVID-19 is "(a) employment as a health professional; (b) employment, of any
-- kind, in a hospital, medical practice, clinic or facility where persons attend for health-related screening, testing or
-- treatment; (c) employment as an ambulance officer". (3) "Despite regulation 7", the injury day is the day the worker is
-- diagnosed by a medical practitioner "on the basis of a test result described in subregulation (4)" (NATA-accredited
-- nucleic acid detection, culture with confirmation, or antibodies), or the day of death if the worker dies of COVID-19
-- before being so diagnosed. (5) "Despite regulation 8, section 10(2) of the Act does not apply ... unless -- (a) the day
-- ... is on or after 16 February 2020; and (b) the worker works or worked in prescribed employment for COVID-19 on the day
-- on which the worker is taken ... to have suffered the injury."
-- A living worker never diagnosed on a qualifying test result has no reg 9(3) day, so reg 9(5) is not met (fork F5).
@export Is my COVID-19 taken to be from my employment under s 10 of the Act (reg 9)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A `COVID-19 employment` @desc The kind of work you were doing on the day you are taken to have caught COVID-19
      `I was diagnosed on a qualifying test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical practitioner diagnosed you with COVID-19 on the basis of a test by a NATA-accredited laboratory (nucleic acid test, cell culture confirmed by nucleic acid test, or antibodies)
      `the day of that diagnosis` IS A DATE @desc The day of that diagnosis (any day if none)
      `the worker died of COVID-19 before such a diagnosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died of COVID-19 before being diagnosed on such a test
      `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day of death (any day if the worker has not died)
      `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has proved to an arbitrator that the injury was not from that employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my COVID-19 taken to be from my employment` IF
        `the work is prescribed`
    AND (`the worker died of COVID-19 before such a diagnosis` OR `I was diagnosed on a qualifying test`)
    AND `the injury day` `is on or after` (`the calendar date` 16 2 2020)
    AND (NOT `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment`)
    WHERE
        `the work is prescribed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my work`
            WHEN `other work` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the injury day` MEANS
            IF `the worker died of COVID-19 before such a diagnosis`
            THEN `the day the worker died`
            ELSE `the day of that diagnosis`

§§ `reg 10 -- post-traumatic stress disorder`

DECLARE `PTSD employment` IS ONE OF
    `a paramedic`
    `an ambulance officer`
    `an ambulance emergency communications officer`
    `Crown employment in a firefighter classification under a firefighting award or agreement`
    `a communications systems officer receiving calls and dispatching emergency services for the fire and emergency services department`
    `other work`

-- Reg 10(2): prescribed employment for post-traumatic stress disorder is "(a) employment as a paramedic; (b) employment as
-- an ambulance officer; (c) employment as an ambulance emergency communications officer; (d) employment by or under the
-- Crown -- (i) to which an industrial award or industrial agreement relating to firefighting applies; and (ii) that is in
-- a firefighter classification ...; (e) employment as a communications systems officer". (3) "Despite regulation 8,
-- section 10(2) of the Act does not apply ... unless -- (a) the worker is diagnosed as having post-traumatic stress
-- disorder by a psychiatrist in accordance with the diagnostic criteria in DSM-5 ...; and (b) [for (2)(a), (b) or (c)] --
-- the worker is first diagnosed ... (whether in accordance with paragraph (a) or otherwise) on or after 1 February 2022;
-- and (c) [for (2)(d) or (e)] -- ... on or after 6 May 2023." Schedule 1 item 37 states no qualifying period.
@export Is my post-traumatic stress disorder taken to be from my employment under s 10 of the Act (reg 10)?
GIVEN `my work` IS A `PTSD employment` @desc The kind of work you do or did
      `a psychiatrist diagnosed me under DSM-5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a psychiatrist has diagnosed you with post-traumatic stress disorder using the DSM-5 diagnostic criteria
      `the day I was first diagnosed` IS A DATE @desc The day you were first diagnosed with post-traumatic stress disorder, by anyone
      `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has proved to an arbitrator that the injury was not from that employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my PTSD taken to be from my employment` IF
        `a psychiatrist diagnosed me under DSM-5`
    AND `the first diagnosis is on or after the start day for my work`
    AND (NOT `my employer proves the injury was not from that employment`)
    WHERE
        `the first diagnosis is on or after the start day for my work` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my work`
            WHEN `a paramedic` THEN `from` (`the calendar date` 1 2 2022)
            WHEN `an ambulance officer` THEN `from` (`the calendar date` 1 2 2022)
            WHEN `an ambulance emergency communications officer` THEN `from` (`the calendar date` 1 2 2022)
            WHEN `Crown employment in a firefighter classification under a firefighting award or agreement` THEN `from` (`the calendar date` 6 5 2023)
            WHEN `a communications systems officer receiving calls and dispatching emergency services for the fire and emergency services department` THEN `from` (`the calendar date` 6 5 2023)
            WHEN `other work` THEN FALSE
        GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `from` `the start` MEANS `the day I was first diagnosed` `is on or after` `the start`

§§ `reg 11 -- cancers added to the firefighter diseases`

DECLARE `Firefighter cancer` IS ONE OF
    `Malignant mesothelioma`
    `Primary site cervical cancer`
    `Primary site lung cancer`
    `Primary site ovarian cancer`
    `Primary site pancreatic cancer`
    `Primary site penile cancer`
    `Primary site skin cancer`
    `Primary site thyroid cancer`
    `A cancer not in the reg 11 Table`

-- Reg 11(1): "a cancer specified in column 1 of an item of the Table is a firefighter disease and the period specified in
-- column 2 of that item is the qualifying period for that firefighter disease": mesothelioma 15 years, cervical 10, lung 15,
-- ovarian 10, pancreatic 10, penile 15, skin 15, thyroid 10. The twelve cancers in the Table in s 11(1) of the Act are
-- firefighter diseases by the Act itself and are not answered here: NOTHING.
@export If my cancer is one the regulations add to the firefighter diseases, what is its qualifying period in years (reg 11(1))?
GIVEN `my cancer` IS A `Firefighter cancer` @desc Your cancer, as the reg 11 Table names it (choose "A cancer not in the reg 11 Table" for any other, including those in the Act's own s 11 Table)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the reg 11 qualifying period in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my cancer`
    WHEN `Malignant mesothelioma` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `Primary site cervical cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `Primary site lung cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `Primary site ovarian cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `Primary site pancreatic cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `Primary site penile cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `Primary site skin cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `Primary site thyroid cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `A cancer not in the reg 11 Table` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the Act's s 11 Table, or no firefighter disease)

-- Reg 11(2): "section 11 of the Act does not apply to an injury by a prescribed firefighter disease suffered by a worker
-- unless the day on which the worker's injury by a firefighter disease is taken, under section 11(5) of the Act, to have
-- been suffered is on or after 13 November 2013." JUST FALSE means only that reg 11(2) does not shut s 11 out; the other
-- requirements of s 11 of the Act (firefighting employment for the qualifying period, hazardous fires) are not encoded.
@export Is my injury by a cancer the regulations add to the firefighter diseases too early for s 11 of the Act to apply (reg 11(2))?
GIVEN `my cancer` IS A `Firefighter cancer` @desc Your cancer, as the reg 11 Table names it
      `the day my injury is taken to be suffered under s 11(5)` IS A DATE @desc The day s 11(5) of the Act fixes for your injury (the earlier of the day of first diagnosis and the other days it names)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does reg 11(2) shut out s 11 for my cancer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my cancer`
    WHEN `A cancer not in the reg 11 Table` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit: reg 11(2) speaks only of the cancers the regulations prescribe)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the day my injury is taken to be suffered under s 11(5)` `is before` (`the calendar date` 13 11 2013)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
